WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.290
Calcium forms its compounds in
just one oxidation state: plus two.

2
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.790
Manganese, further along period 4,

3
00:00:07.840 --> 00:00:12.030
forms compounds in every state
from plus two to plus seven.

4
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:14.730
Both are metals, in the same period.

5
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.630
So why such a difference?

6
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:22.230
Why can manganese be plus two to plus
seven, while calcium is only ever plus two?

7
00:00:22.280 --> 00:00:26.250
In this mission, you'll find out what
makes an element a transition element,

8
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:29.230
and meet their characteristic properties.

9
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:31.130
You'll build complex ions from ligands,

10
00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:34.830
and write the configurations
of transition-metal ions.

11
00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:39.470
Your mission: explain why manganese
has so many oxidation states.
